<title>INDIA: Indian soybean in bearish trends, arrivals rise.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean in bearish trends, arrivals rise.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Wednesday showed bearish trend in central region markets with prices down by 150-300 rupees per tonne on increased arrivals against limited demand, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained lower on heavy selling against poor demand. Soyoil solvent was down by 300 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined was down by 200 rupees per tonne. Undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were also easier in local markets and in FOR (Free on Rail) condition, but in export, prices were steady. Soymeal yellow was $320 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $120 per tonnne FAS in bulk for export and was 4,200 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) conditions. The undertone was easy.</p>
